WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.080
Dragon Warrior 2, this is a role playing game filled with adventure and challenges.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:29.900
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.040
I'm Mike.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.220
And I'm Sean.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:35.880
A role playing game filled with adventure and challenges.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.140
Is there a role playing game that isn't?

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:45.040
Yeah, this is one of the more generic ways to pitch a JRPG, I think.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:51.980
And I know that it's a cheap shot because obviously the back of the box also has a bunch of other things about plot and what you'll be doing.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:01:00.060
But it's also like other things that JRPGs talk about with like, you know, evil wizards and getting, you know, getting revenge.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.060
And yeah, that's true.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:05.880
That's true. So I just want to put an emphasis that like that part was in bold.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.460
Okay. So like that is the part that they thought would catch your eye as well.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:16.640
And you have to remember, it's early in the days of RPGs, but it's not that early anymore, right?

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.600
Like we're playing this game in 1990 on the NES.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:22.960
We've played a few chronologically at this point.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.620
But this game actually came out in 97, right?

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:32.340
Right. And so that's what I want to talk to you about, Sean, because there's like so many ways that we could handle this episode.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:38.740
And there's so many ways that people could have experienced Dragon Warrior 2 over the last 30 years.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:44.480
We can view this the way that we view every NES game on nostalgia.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:51.740
And that is just as the 360 whatever episode of the show with no nostalgia.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:55.280
And we're just playing it in real modern time on 2025.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:57.740
And we're just dealing with that.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:03.340
Or we could look at this as like, well, this is the sequel to Dragon Warrior.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:04.620
And how does that fare?

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:08.660
Right. Because like technically that's a big deal in its own, right?

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:16.240
It's like the original Dragon Warrior was not without its faults, but was a big deal for the NES RPG library.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:18.220
And this is now the sequel to that.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:26.400
Or you could look at it as like, well, technically this game Dragon Warrior 2 came out before Final Fantasy 1.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:32.480
