00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:39.600
But is it fair to look at Dragon Warrior 2 after the fact when it technically was made beforehand?

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.240
I get it.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:50.100
But, you know, I think like we haven't been, we haven't been like assigning a rubric that sort of scales as time goes on.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:58.340
You know, this is, I know that we have been taking into account the sort of maturation of genre.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:04.100
But I think like if the game's good enough, regardless of when it came out, it'll make it on there or it won't.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:12.400
Well, especially because so much of the emphasis of my opening read of this show focuses on games releasing in North America.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:20.340
I think it's just really important that we focus on the fact that Dragon Warrior 2 came out here at this point chronologically.

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:27.180
And Final Fantasy really ate a lot of its lunch just coming out a few months beforehand.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:36.840
Because, holy shit, are there so many features in Dragon Warrior 2 that are obviously like quality of life boosts over the original game.

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:40.380
But just like now it's not even worth talking about, right?

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:43.360
Like we're going to talk about that now there's a party, right?

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:45.600
But there was a party in Final Fantasy.

